{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ThLuTfqbdbWsNDSVQyQ8kw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient measurement temperature dependence Murday Cotts NMR\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"link.springer.com\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553\"},{\"title\":\"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion coefficients of ionic liquids measured by multinuclear benchtop NMR\",\"url\":\"https://magritek.com/?p=21016\"},{\"title\":\"s00231 011 0874 9\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9\"},{\"title\":\"subject:Self diffusion coefficients\",\"url\":\"https://fitforthem.unipa.it/subject:Self-diffusion coefficients\"},{\"title\":\"link.aps.org\",\"url\":\"https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PhysRevB.83.094302\"},{\"title\":\"www.rsc.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.rsc.org/suppdata/d3/cp/d3cp04666d/d3cp04666d1.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Pulsed field gradient magnetic resonance measurements of lithium-ion diffusion\",\"url\":\"https://dspace.mit.edu/entities/publication/104d2ab7-993c-4471-ba74-3523459e31b6\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion and isotopic effects in liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scilit.com/publications/a87ad4db2680c466d4fc33f00ce090a5\"},{\"title\":\"next.sciencegate.app\",\"url\":\"https://next.sciencegate.app/document/10.1557/opl.2012.1517\"}]\n\nThe search did not return the Murday and Cotts data itself, so I can't give you their measured values or fitted temperature dependence.\n\n- **The original paper:** A bibliography lists Murday and Cotts, \"Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium,\" *J. Chem. Phys.* 48:4938–4945 (1968). Murday JS, Cotts RM (1968) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium. J Chem Phys 48:4938–4945 is the reference for this work.\n- **Later simulation work:** A 2012 molecular-dynamics study using an EAM potential reports that the liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient increases with temperature increasing and decreases with pressure increasing. The same authors say their computed values are in good agreement with Murday's experiment results in atmosphere. They also derived an Arrhenius-form fit from their simulations (We get the Arrhenius equation according to the simulation results.).\n- **Isotope effects:** A 1986 theory paper in *Philosophical Magazine A* addresses liquid lithium self-diffusion and explains the anomalous ratio between the self-diffusion coefficients of Li6 and Li7 through the mass dependence of the atomic mean free path.\n- **Related but not on point:** A Springer paper on 7Li nuclear spin relaxation time T1 in solid lithium cites Murday and Cotts (1971) among other NMR work, but it concerns the solid phase.\n\nTo get the actual Murday–Cotts coefficients and temperature range, I'd need the 1968 J. Chem. Phys. paper itself, or a later review that tabulates its values.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b807e1-288c-43fd-b0e9-80dfc39ff748","uuid":"52260b8b-3236-4bf1-8f6c-d4c4792446e7","timestamp":"2026-11-01T04:00:02.465Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient measurement temperature dependence Murday Cotts NMR","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01RndiDyqRpHjhf5jNftbVdi","content":[{"title":"link.springer.com","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553"},{"title":"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium","url":"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/"},{"title":"Self-diffusion coefficients of ionic liquids measured by multinuclear benchtop NMR","url":"https://magritek.com/?p=21016"},{"title":"s00231 011 0874 9","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.10