{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SqaPnPZCTo54K85eadPfqH","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient cm2/s experimental values 800 K density 0.48 g/cm3\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Investigations of diffusion processes in liquid lithium and lithium-hydrogen melt by quasielastic neutron scattering (Journal Article)\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/etdeweb/biblio/21180951\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/289594580_Self-diffusion_coefficient_of_liquid_lithium\"},{\"title\":\"Self-Diffusion Coefficient of Liquid Lithium - ADS\",\"url\":\"http://adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1968JChPh..48.4938M\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium (Journal Article)\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/etdeweb/biblio/21547860\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225135828_Self-diffusion_coefficient_study_of_liquid_lithium\"},{\"title\":\"Diffusion of lithium ions in Lithium-argyrodite solid-state electrolytes\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-020-00432-1\"},{\"title\":\"Isotope effect for the self-diffusion in liquid lithium and tin; Izotopnyj ehffekt pri samodiffuzii v zhidkhkh litii i olove (Journal Article)\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/etdeweb/biblio/20363411\"},{\"title\":\"Lithium Intercalation in the Anisotropic van der Waals Magnetic Semiconductor CrSBr\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.15663\"},{\"title\":\"An ion-microprobe study of the self-diffusion of Li+ of lithium fluoride: The Philosophical Magazine: A Journal of Theoretical Experimental and Applied Physics: Vol 29, No 3\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/14786437408213232\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up a direct experimental value at 800 K, and nothing in the results addresses the 0.48 g/cm³ density.\n\n- **Quasielastic neutron scattering (JINR Dubna):** Measurements were made on liquid lithium at 500 K and 830 K. The authors report that the self-diffusion coefficient agrees with literature values. The results don't include the numbers themselves in the excerpt. experiments on liquid lithium (at 500 K and 830 K) and lithium-hydrogen melt were run on the DIN-2PI spectrometer. (The self-diffusion coefficient in liquid lithium obtained for both temperatures is in the agreement with the one known in literature.)\n- **NMR (Murday and Cohen, 1968, J. Chem. Phys.):** This is the classic reference. At the melting point D = 6.8 ± 0.3 × 10-5 cm2/sec. The activation fit is D = 0.94 ± 0.4 × 10-3 exp [ - (2300 ± 300 cal) / RT ] cm2 / sec.\n\nEvaluating that Arrhenius fit at 800 K (my own arithmetic, not a value stated in the source) gives roughly 2 × 10⁻⁴ cm²/s. That is consistent with the melting-point value, but the fit carries sizeable uncertainties.\n\n- **Molecular dynamics (Belashchenko et al.):** Simulations at 470 K reportedly gained satisfactory agreement with experimental data.\n\nFor a true 800 K experimental value and a density check at 0.48 g/cm³, I'd look at the original Murday–Cohen paper and a liquid-metal property compilation, since the search results didn't cover either.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b807e1-288c-43fd-b0e9-80dfc39ff748","uuid":"d3b5e613-cf46-42cf-8e52-d56838a3b6f7","timestamp":"2026-11-01T04:00:48.946Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient cm2/s experimental values 800 K density 0.48 g/cm3","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01TWE9hagY2U2XoE2mY7RXtU","content":[{"title":"Investigations of diffusion processes in liquid lithium and lithium-hydrogen melt by quasielastic neutron scattering (Journal Article)","url":"https://www.osti.gov/etdeweb/biblio/21180951"},{"title":"(PDF) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/289594580_Self-diffusion_coefficient_of_liquid_lithium"},{"title":"Self-Diffusion Coefficient of Liquid Lithium - ADS","url":"http://adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1968JChPh..48.4938M"},{"title":"Self-diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium (Journal Article)","url":"https://www.osti.gov/etdeweb/biblio/21547860"},{"title":"Self-diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225135828_Self-diffusion_coefficient_study_of_liquid_lithium"},{"title":"Diffusion of lithium ions in Lithium-argyrodite solid-state electrolytes","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41524-020-00432-1"},{"title":"Isotope effect for the self-diffusion in liquid lithium and tin; Izotopnyj ehffekt pri samodiffuzii v zhidkhkh litii i olove (Journal Article)","url":"https://www.osti.gov/etdeweb/biblio/20363411"},{"title":"Lithium Intercalation in the Anisotropic van der Waals Magnetic Semiconductor CrSBr","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.15663"},{"title":"An ion-microprobe study of the self-diffusion of Li+ of lithium fluoride: The Philosophical Magazine: A Journal of Theoretical Experimental and Applied Physics: Vol 29, No 3","url":"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/14786437408213232"}]},"The search didn't turn up a direct experimental value at 800 K, and nothing in the results addresses the 0.48 g/cm³ density.\n\n- **Quasielastic neutron scattering (JINR Dubna):** Measurements were made on liquid lithium at 500 K and 830 K. The authors report that the self-diffusion coefficient agrees with literature values. The results don't include the numbers themselves in the excerpt. experiments on liquid lithium (at 500 K and 830 K) and lithium-hydrogen melt were run on the DIN-2PI spectrometer. (The self-diffusion coefficient in liquid lithium obtained for both temperatures is in the agreement with the one known in literature.)\n- **NMR (Murday and Cohen, 1968, J. Chem. Phys.):** This is the classic reference. At the melting point D = 6.8 ± 0.3 × 10-5 cm2/sec. The activation fit is D = 0.94 ± 0.4 × 10-3 exp [ - (2300 ± 300 cal) / RT ] cm2 / sec.\n\nEvaluating that Arrhenius fit at 800 K (my own arithmetic, not a value stated in the source) gives roughly 2 × 10⁻⁴ cm²/s. That is consistent with the melting-point value, but the fit carries sizeable uncertainties.\n\n- **Molecular dynamics (Belashchenko et al.):** Simulations at 470 K reportedly gained satisfactory agreement with experimental data.\n\nFor a true 800 K experimental value and a density check at 0.48 g/cm³, I'd look at the original Murday–Cohen paper and a liquid-metal property compilation, since the search results didn't cover either."],"durationSeconds":5.9873905550000055,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SqaPnPZCTo54K85eadPfqH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
