{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HgMVPo8wsZGRVAfGQ33a2c","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium density temperature correlation kg/m3 Davison 1968 OR Ohse handbook lithium density formula\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Yamdb: easily accessible thermophysical properties of liquid metals and molten salts\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2402.10922\"},{\"title\":\"ntrs.nasa.gov\",\"url\":\"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19680018893/downloads/19680018893.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ntrs.nasa.gov\",\"url\":\"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19680018893\"},{\"title\":\"Operational conditions:\",\"url\":\"https://www.chemeo.com/mid/22-277-a/Choline-chloride_Urea_lithium-chloride\"},{\"title\":\"ntrs.nasa.gov\",\"url\":\"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/archive/nasa/casi.ntrs.nasa.gov/19680018893.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"lithium chloride Water\",\"url\":\"https://www.chemeo.com/mid/10-192-h/lithium-chloride_Water\"},{\"title\":\"densite et temperature de cristallisation d une solution aqueuse de 22391\",\"url\":\"https://iifiir.org/fr/fridoc/densite-et-temperature-de-cristallisation-d-une-solution-aqueuse-de-22391\"},{\"title\":\"ntlib.org.cn\",\"url\":\"https://ntlib.org.cn/asset/detail/0/20339351323\"},{\"title\":\"Operational condition: Pressure, kPa = 101 (Liquid)\",\"url\":\"https://www.chemeo.com/mid/24-464-a/Sucrose_Water_Lithium-sulfate\"},{\"title\":\"lithium bromide Methyl Alcohol\",\"url\":\"https://chemeo.com/mid/12-510-b/lithium-bromide_Methyl-Alcohol\"}]\n\nI didn't find the explicit Davison or Ohse density formula in these results, so I can't give you coefficients. Here's what the search did turn up:\n\n- **Davison (NASA TN D-4650, 1968):** This compilation fits polynomials to literature data and chose a linear form for density. The report explains that a cubic fit would give a minimum near 1600 K, and that a monatomic liquid has no clear physical reason to gain density near its boiling point, so the linear form was kept. The report describes fitting a polynomial to experimental data obtained from the literature. The search excerpt doesn't include the actual density equation or its coefficients, so you'll need the full PDF (ntrs.nasa.gov, document 19680018893) for those.\n- **Ohse (1985) via Yamdb:** A tabulated reference value for lithium density at 800 K is 483.21 kg/m³, attributed to Ohse (1985). The Yamdb table lists this as the density value at 800 K from Ohse (1985). This is a single data point, not a correlation, but it can serve as a sanity check for any formula you derive.\n\nTo get the correlation itself, check the full Davison report for the density equation, and look at Ohse's 1985 handbook (or the Yamdb source code, which implements Ohse-based property equations) for the temperature-dependent form.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b807e1-288c-43fd-b0e9-80dfc39ff748","uuid":"3a5bdc09-bfb6-4c19-9913-13457b651096","timestamp":"2026-11-01T04:01:07.168Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium density temperature correlation kg/m3 Davison 1968 OR Ohse handbook lithium density formula","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01UgpqvkPMEfTNFcFzMT8Kw8","content":[{"title":"Yamdb: easily accessible thermophysical properties of liquid metals and molten salts","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2402.10922"},{"title":"ntrs.nasa.gov","url":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19680018893/downloads/19680018893.pdf"},{"title":"ntrs.nasa.gov","url":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19680018893"},{"title":"Operational conditions:","url":"https://www.chemeo.com/mid/22-277-a/Choline-chloride_Urea_lithium-chloride"},{"title":"ntrs.nasa.gov","url":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/archive/nasa/casi.ntrs.nasa.gov/19680018893.pdf"},{"title":"lithium chloride Water","url":"https://www.chemeo.com/mid/10-192-h/lithium-chloride_Water"},{"title":"densite et temperature de cristal