ion beyond the NMR range; the Murday-Cotts numbers were taken from a search-result abstract summary, the paper itself was not retrieved). Single trajectory, fixed density (no NPT check of model density), PBE-trained universal potential.\"}\nEOF\nR=$(./board post property_result @/work/run/result.json --parent 8fe243a6-bf82-4e43-a880-717fe00863bc | awk '{print $NF}'); echo $R\n./board post check '{\"check_type\": \"independent_known_result\", \"verdict\": \"pass_within_uncertainty\", \"note\": \"Same setup (MACE-MP-0, 250 atoms, Langevin melt/equil then 20 ps NVE, dt 1 fs) at 470 K target (NVE <T> = 458 K, density 0.5133 g/cm3 from the same Ohse-form correlation): D = 5.9e-5 cm2/s (block SEM 0.3e-5), vs measured NMR 6.8 +/- 0.3e-5 cm2/s at Tm=453.7 K (Murday & Cotts, J. Chem. Phys. 48, 4938 (1968)). Model ~13% low before finite-size correction; finite-size correction (~+10-20%) would close most of the gap. NVE energy drift -1.8e-4 meV/atom/ps. Energy-conservation check of the 800 K production: drift 1.3e-4 meV/atom/ps - pass.\"}' --parent $R","description":"Post property result and validation check"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":62130,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":953,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14b807e1-288c-43fd-b0e9-80dfc39ff748","uuid":"80ac064b-e2dc-40d5-a466-614e659dc918","timestamp":"2026-11-01T04:46:08.017Z","request_id":"req_011CgbbkjaxQ3UxTyVxj2YBT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018i22tQpFd7bCxjLYrWC9bf":{"command":"cd /work && cat > /work/run/result.json <<'EOF'\n{\"candidate\": \"lithium (liquid)\", \"family\": \"alkali metal\", \"tier\": \"trust\", \"property\": \"self_diffusion\"